.TH FASTRDP-TERMSRV-KEYTAB 8 "October 2026" "fast-rdp-server" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
fastrdp-termsrv-keytab \- copy the TERMSRV keys of the host keytab for the fastrdp proxy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fastrdp-termsrv-keytab
.RB [ \-s
.IR host-keytab ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR termsrv-keytab ]
.RB [ \-g
.IR group ]
.RB [ \-n ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
On Active Directory hosts the machine account owns the
.B TERMSRV/*
service principals, so their keys are in the host keytab, which the unprivileged
proxy must not read.
.B fastrdp-termsrv-keytab
writes a keytab with only the
.B TERMSRV/*
entries (owner root, the given group, mode 0640) and replaces the old one
atomically. It fails if the host keytab has no TERMSRV keys.
.PP
It also copies the entries of the machine account itself
.RI ( NAME $@ REALM )
whose key version, encryption type and key equal those of a TERMSRV entry.
Active Directory keeps one key set per account, so these are the TERMSRV keys
under the account's own name and the proxy gets no new key. Windows clients
(mstsc under CredSSP) start with Kerberos user-to-user, and the proxy must then
answer with a TGT of the account that owns the TERMSRV name, which it gets with
these entries. Without them Windows clients cannot log in with Kerberos; the
command prints a note when it finds none.
.PP
sssd changes the machine password regularly, which writes new keys to the host
keytab.
.B fastrdp-termsrv-keytab.path
watches
.I /etc/krb5.keytab
and starts
.BR fastrdp-termsrv-keytab.service ,
which runs this command and restarts
.B fastrdp-proxy.service
if it is running. Both units are installed disabled; on AD hosts run
.B systemctl enable \-\-now fastrdp-termsrv-keytab.path
once. FreeIPA and other KDCs have separate TERMSRV keys and need neither.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-s " host-keytab"
Keytab to copy from (FASTRDP_HOST_KEYTAB, default
.IR /etc/krb5.keytab ).
.TP
.BI \-d " termsrv-keytab"
Keytab to write (FASTRDP_TERMSRV_KEYTAB, default
.IR /etc/fastrdp/termsrv.keytab ).
.TP
.BI \-g " group"
Group of the written keytab (FASTRDP_TERMSRV_KEYTAB_GROUP, default
.IR _fastrdp-proxy ).
.TP
.B \-n
Copy the TERMSRV entries only, not the machine account's
(FASTRDP_TERMSRV_KEYTAB_MACHINE=no; default yes).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Options win over the environment variables named above, which win over
the configuration file.
.B FASTRDP_TERMSRV_CONF
names another configuration file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/fastrdp/termsrv.conf
.IB KEY = VALUE
settings, shared with
.BR fastrdp-termsrv-check (8).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 written, 1 no TERMSRV keys or an error, 2 usage.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fastrdp-termsrv-check (8),
.BR ktutil (1),
.BR adcli (8)
